    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (25 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and derived fields are computed in the MapStruct mapper (like the existing `membershipNumber`, `displayName`, etc.), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\nThis follows the spec exactly: `namesakeCount` is set at create time from `countNamesakes(...)`, and `email` is `null` when absent (blank normalizes to null in `normalizeEmail`), so the tier is `SILVER` only for a unique owner (namesakeCount 0) who supplied an email, and `BRONZE` otherwise. Both new `Cp15Tests` cases and all 25 existing tests pass.",
